enichyar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-07-28T15:08:51Z","updated_at":"2015-07-28T15:08:51Z","body":"@klimov-paul, thank you!\n\nI use same regexp as temporary solution: `page/<slug:((?!index).)*>`. But it doesn't work properly if slug has word \"index\". For example: `index1`, `indexation`, etc.\n\n> It seems 'create URL cache' feature should be reverted (which whould be a pity) or made optional.\n\nI think 'create URL cache' was good idea. If there is no issue with this feature except my issue I propose to not revert this feature and add an ability to make inversed regexp in url.\n\nFor example:\n`page/<slug:!index>` — All except \"index\"\n`page/<slug:!(index|sitemap|contacts)>` — All except \"index\", \"sitemap\", \"contacts\"\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yiisoft/yii2/issues/comments/125642257/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"genichyar","id":3851611,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTE2MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3851611?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar","html_url":"https://github.com/genichyar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/genichyar/followers","following_url":"https:/